    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: server-assigned `customerCode`\n\nThe spec required assigning `customerCode` formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` on owner creation, where LAST3 is the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` and NNNN is a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count.\n\nSince the acceptance test reads the code back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, the value must be **persisted**, so the change spans the entity, DB, DTO, and the OfficeFloor pipeline:\n\n1. **New pipeline step** \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode.java` computes the code from `@Val Owner` and `ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1`, then sets it on the entity. Wired into `owners.POST.yml` between `build` and `save` (under `govern: [ transaction ]`). Because each MockMvc request runs in the test's shared transaction, Hibernate auto-flushes before the count query, so the second owner sees the first \u2014 giving the `cb == ca + 1` the test asserts.\n\n2. **Entity** \u2014 added `customerCode` field (`customer_code` column) with getter/setter to `Owner`.\n\n3. **Persistence** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) and appended `NULL` to the positional seed `INSERT`s in the hsqldb and mysql `data.sql` (the column-listed h2/postgres inserts needed no change).\n\n4. **API/DTO** \u2014 added `customerCode` as a `readOnly` property on the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`; the generated `OwnerDto` field is mapped automatically by MapStruct (name match), so both the create response and GET return it.\n\n`PUT`/update paths are unaffected: `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` doesn't touch `customerCode`, and `ApplyOwner` mutates the loaded entity in place, preserving the stored code.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS (this repo contains a single test class, `AcceptanceTest`).",
